    {
      "id": "claim_14fd3e9407164f668f9461dd49a671a3",
      "statement": "The `oifs create` command with `--encrypt` flag creates an encrypted OIFS image by generating a cryptographically secure 16-byte random salt, deriving a 256-bit master key from the password via Argon2id (m=64MiB, t=3, p=4), immediately deriving four domain-separated 256-bit subkeys via BLAKE2b-512 (payload_key, filename_siv_key, filename_cipher_key, ipc_auth_key), and initializing the filesystem with context-bound AEAD (encryption_version=2). Password is obtained from --password, OIFS_PASSWORD, or interactive prompt with confirmation; JSON mode requires explicit password. The --journal flag enables metadata journaling.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bin/oifs.rs#L706-L761",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:872e32ceaf074b2a42b3aca99a11165c5fd0fe8dd037a5a2afd1d682e1eb89bd:"
